 A formation that senses, predicts, chooses, acts and revises is one law within the unfolding, not a subject facing a world: its internal part reads what goes on through what it senses, and what it does is part of what goes on ([§1](#r-the-markov-blanket-as-a-coupling-structure)). Six laws state that loop under their premises: when a reading of the world is kept by the formation's own update, and which reading its own history carries; what a course chosen through a model tests of the laws it keeps; what acts cannot tell of a model and an order; when a prediction read by what it predicts is right; what holding an act for a reading is worth on the formation's own model; and what informing the reading formation and revaluing it do to that worth. What a reader of the loop's acts fixes of it is [§11](#what-the-acts-show)'s.
 
 <a id="r-a-reading-kept-by-its-update"></a>
-**Theorem** (root for closure: any carrier and relation; any types for the loop; near-definitional, with one general law). *A reading kept by its update, and the reading its own history carries.* A region kept along every finite reach of a relation is a closed region, and conversely (`ReadingLoop.kept_iff_closed`, by `«闭之及»`). On one carrier of world and state, let the world become what a relation admits under the act its state gives and the state be updated from that act and the value sensed (`ReadingLoop.joint`). Where a supplied reading of the world by the state is kept by the update under every act (`ReadingLoop.KeptBy`), a policy keeps a task at every configuration reached from one where the reading holds, and goes on from each such configuration, exactly where each state's act can be taken at every world its reading admits and leads only where the task holds (`ReadingLoop.keeps_continues_iff`); successor safety alone (`ReadingLoop.keeps_iff_good`) is met by an act no world can take. Given choice over the states, such a policy exists exactly where each state has one such act (`ReadingLoop.keeping_policy_iff`). Acts good for every two worlds a reading admits need not be one act good for all (`ReadingLoop.PairwiseShared.two_share`, `ReadingLoop.PairwiseShared.none_for_all`), and being kept is not being informative: the readings of every world and of none are kept by every update (`ReadingLoop.everything_kept`, `ReadingLoop.nothing_kept`, `ReadingLoop.nothing_sound`). With the state the history of acts and values sensed, the worlds possible after a history are kept by recording and are the least reading so kept that holds at the starts (`ReadingLoop.possible_kept`, `ReadingLoop.possible_least`); a policy acting from its history keeps a task at every configuration reached from a start exactly where, at every history it generates, its act leads only where the task holds from every world possible after it, and goes on exactly where its act can be taken at each (`ReadingLoop.history_keeps_iff`, `ReadingLoop.history_continues_iff`). These verify a given policy; a condition for one to exist that ties histories to the task's futures is not proved ([record](../results/records/a-reading-kept-by-its-update.md)).
+**Theorem** (root for closure: any carrier and relation; any types for the loop; near-definitional, with one general law). *A reading kept by its update, and the reading its own history carries.* A region kept along every finite reach of a relation is a closed region, and conversely (`ReadingLoop.kept_iff_closed`, by `«闭之及»`). On one carrier of world and state, let the world become what a relation admits under the act its state gives and the state be updated from that act and the value sensed (`ReadingLoop.joint`). Where a supplied reading of the world by the state is kept by the update under every act (`ReadingLoop.KeptBy`), a policy keeps a task at every configuration reached from one where the reading holds, and goes on from each such configuration, exactly where each state's act can be taken at every world its reading admits and leads only where the task holds (`ReadingLoop.keeps_continues_iff`); successor safety alone (`ReadingLoop.keeps_iff_leadsInto`) is met by an act no world can take. Given choice over the states, such a policy exists exactly where each state has one such act (`ReadingLoop.keeping_policy_iff`). Acts leading into the task from every two worlds a reading admits need not be one act leading into it from all (`ReadingLoop.PairwiseShared.two_share`, `ReadingLoop.PairwiseShared.none_for_all`), and being kept is not being informative: the readings of every world and of none are kept by every update (`ReadingLoop.everything_kept`, `ReadingLoop.nothing_kept`, `ReadingLoop.nothing_sound`). With the state the history of acts and values sensed, the worlds possible after a history are kept by recording and are the least reading so kept that holds at the starts (`ReadingLoop.possible_kept`, `ReadingLoop.possible_least`); a policy acting from its history keeps a task at every configuration reached from a start exactly where, at every history it generates, its act leads only where the task holds from every world possible after it, and goes on exactly where its act can be taken at each (`ReadingLoop.history_keeps_iff`, `ReadingLoop.history_continues_iff`). These verify a given policy; a condition for one to exist that ties histories to the task's futures is not proved ([record](../results/records/a-reading-kept-by-its-update.md)).
 
-**Reading** [AI reading, new]. The law is a safety composition, related to possibilistic belief interpretations of regulation (Virgo, Biehl, Baltieri and Capucci 2025), whose closure is under the policy chosen, as `keeps_of_good` takes it, where `KeptBy` asks it under every act; with [§9](#r-when-to-inquire-and-when-to-respond)'s choice from readings it is requisite variety along a loop. The good regulator theorem of Conant and Ashby (1970) concerns simplest optimal regulation; nothing of optimality or of a regulator's having to model what it regulates is proved here. The history form says what a regulator acting from what couples in must meet: safety and enabledness at every world compatible with its own history and the starts. A coarser reading can suffice where its further worlds ask compatible acts.
